Git in Termux - Installation and Usage Guide
=============================================


========================================
INSTALLATION
========================================

Step 1: Update packages
-----------------------
    pkg update && pkg upgrade

Step 2: Install Git
-------------------
    pkg install git

Step 3: Verify installation
----------------------------
    git --version


========================================
FIRST TIME SETUP
========================================

Set your name and email (required before committing):

    git config --global user.name "Your Name"
    git config --global user.email "you@example.com"

Set default branch name to main:

    git config --global init.defaultBranch main

Check your config:

    git config --list


========================================
SSH KEY SETUP (for GitHub/GitLab)
========================================

Step 1: Install openssh
-----------------------
    pkg install openssh

Step 2: Generate SSH key
------------------------
    ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "you@example.com"
    (Press Enter to accept defaults)

Step 3: View your public key
-----------------------------
    cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

Step 4: Add key to GitHub
--------------------------
    1. Copy the output of the above command
    2. Go to GitHub -> Settings -> SSH and GPG keys
    3. Click "New SSH key"
    4. Paste your key and save

Step 5: Test connection
------------------------
    ssh -T git@github.com


========================================
BASIC GIT WORKFLOW
========================================

CREATE A NEW REPOSITORY
------------------------
    mkdir myproject
    cd myproject
    git init

CLONE AN EXISTING REPOSITORY
------------------------------
    git clone https://github.com/username/repo.git

    # or using SSH (after setting up SSH key):
    git clone git@github.com:username/repo.git

CHECK STATUS
------------
    git status

ADD FILES (stage changes)
--------------------------
    git add filename.txt        # add a specific file
    git add .                   # add all changed files
    git add *.py                # add all .py files

COMMIT CHANGES
--------------
    git commit -m "Your commit message here"

VIEW COMMIT HISTORY
--------------------
    git log                     # full log
    git log --oneline           # compact log
    git log --oneline -10       # last 10 commits

PUSH TO REMOTE
--------------
    git push                    # push current branch
    git push origin main        # push main branch
    git push -u origin main     # push and set upstream

PULL FROM REMOTE
-----------------
    git pull                    # pull current branch
    git pull origin main        # pull from main


========================================
BRANCHING
========================================

LIST BRANCHES
--------------
    git branch                  # local branches
    git branch -a               # all branches (including remote)

CREATE A BRANCH
----------------
    git branch new-feature

SWITCH TO A BRANCH
-------------------
    git checkout new-feature
    # or newer syntax:
    git switch new-feature

CREATE AND SWITCH IN ONE STEP
------------------------------
    git checkout -b new-feature
    # or newer syntax:
    git switch -c new-feature

MERGE A BRANCH
---------------
    git checkout main
    git merge new-feature

DELETE A BRANCH
----------------
    git branch -d new-feature          # safe delete
    git branch -D new-feature          # force delete
    git push origin --delete new-feature  # delete remote branch


========================================
UNDOING CHANGES
========================================

DISCARD UNSTAGED CHANGES
-------------------------
    git restore filename.txt    # restore a file
    git restore .               # restore all files

UNSTAGE A FILE
---------------
    git restore --staged filename.txt

UNDO LAST COMMIT (keep changes)
---------------------------------
    git reset --soft HEAD~1

UNDO LAST COMMIT (discard changes)
------------------------------------
    git reset --hard HEAD~1

REVERT A COMMIT (safe, creates new commit)
-------------------------------------------
    git revert <commit-hash>


========================================
VIEWING DIFFERENCES
========================================

    git diff                    # unstaged changes
    git diff --staged           # staged changes
    git diff main..feature      # between branches
    git show <commit-hash>      # changes in a commit


========================================
WORKING WITH REMOTE REPOSITORIES
========================================

VIEW REMOTES
-------------
    git remote -v

ADD A REMOTE
-------------
    git remote add origin https://github.com/user/repo.git

CHANGE REMOTE URL
------------------
    git remote set-url origin git@github.com:user/repo.git

FETCH CHANGES (without merging)
---------------------------------
    git fetch origin

UPDATE LOCAL BRANCH LIST
--------------------------
    git fetch --prune


========================================
.GITIGNORE
========================================

Create a .gitignore file to exclude files from tracking:

    nano .gitignore

Common entries:
    __pycache__/
    *.pyc
    .env
    node_modules/
    *.log
    .DS_Store

After creating .gitignore:
    git add .gitignore
    git commit -m "Add .gitignore"


========================================
USEFUL SHORTCUTS & TIPS
========================================

    git status -s               # short status output
    git log --oneline --graph   # visual branch graph
    git stash                   # temporarily save changes
    git stash pop               # restore stashed changes
    git cherry-pick <hash>      # apply a specific commit
    git blame filename.txt      # see who changed each line
    git grep "search term"      # search inside tracked files

ALIASES (optional shortcuts)
------------------------------
    git config --global alias.st status
    git config --global alias.co checkout
    git config --global alias.br branch
    git config --global alias.lg "log --oneline --graph"

    # Usage:
    git st      # same as git status
    git co main # same as git checkout main
    git lg      # pretty log graph


========================================
COMMON ERRORS & FIXES
========================================

"Please tell me who you are"
    -> git config --global user.name "Name"
    -> git config --global user.email "email"

"Permission denied (publickey)"
    -> Set up SSH key (see SSH KEY SETUP section above)

"fatal: not a git repository"
    -> Run 'git init' or 'cd' into your repo folder

"rejected - non-fast-forward"
    -> git pull origin main --rebase
    -> Then push again

"merge conflict"
    -> Open the conflicted file, fix the <<<<< ===== >>>>> markers
    -> git add .
    -> git commit

Authentication failed (HTTPS)
    -> Use SSH instead, or use a Personal Access Token
    -> GitHub no longer accepts passwords for HTTPS
